{"name":"Arbor Vitae","hex":"#bbc3ad","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arbor vitae","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of arborvitae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arbor_vitae"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arbor vitae (anatomy)","blocks":[{"text":"The arbor vitae is the cerebellar white matter, so called for its branched, tree-like appearance. In some ways it more closely resembles a fern, and is present in both cerebellar hemispheres. The pattern is most apparent on a midsagittal section of the cerebellum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Arbor_Vitae_in_the_Human_Cerebellum.svg/330px-Arbor_Vitae_in_the_Human_Cerebellum.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arbor_vitae_(anatomy)"},{"title":"List of phrases containing the word vitae","blocks":[{"text":"Vitae is a Latin word, meaning or pertaining to life."},{"items":["Aqua vitae, archaic name for a concentrated aqueous solution of ethanol, distilled spirits","Arbor vitae (disambiguation), \"tree of life\"","De Brevitate Vitae, work of Roman philosopher Seneca","Curriculum vitae or CV, summary of education and job experience, résumé","Deus Vitae, manga series created by Takuya Fujima","Evangelium Vitae, encyclical by Pope John Paul II","Humanae vitae, encyclical by Pope Paul VI","Liber Vitae, medieval confraternity book","Lignum vitae, species of plant in the creosote bush family","Magistra vitae, Latin expression from Cicero's De Oratore, \"history is life's teacher\"","Non scholae, sed vitae discimus, Latin phrase, \"We do not learn for the school, but for life.\"","Sodalitium Christianae Vitae, society of apostolic life founded by Luis Fernando Figari","Speculum Vitae, Middle English poem possibly by William of Nassyngton","Vitae duorum Offarum, literary history written in the mid-thirteenth century"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_phrases_containing_the_word_vitae"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Arbor_vitae_-_animation.gif/500px-Arbor_vitae_-_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Arbor_vitae_-_animation.gif/500px-Arbor_vitae_-_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArbor_vitae_-_animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png/120px-Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png/250px-Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png/120px-Midline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidline_sagittal_view_of_the_brainstem_and_cerebellum_-_Arbor_vitae.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Slide2qq.JPG/120px-Slide2qq.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Slide2qq.JPG/250px-Slide2qq.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Slide2qq.JPG/120px-Slide2qq.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign